      {q:"Is VELYS better than Mako or ROSA robotic knee replacement?", a:"All major robotic platforms — VELYS, Mako, ROSA, CORI — deliver excellent accuracy in experienced hands. VELYS's main advantages are being imageless (no pre-op CT, no extra radiation), faster surgical workflow, and tight integration with the proven J&J Attune knee implant system."},
      {q:"Do you offer Zimmer ROSA robotic knee replacement or Zimmer knee implants?", a:"At DHS Multispecialty Hospital we perform robotic knee replacement on the VELYS platform from Johnson & Johnson DePuy Synthes with the J&J Attune knee implant — not Zimmer's ROSA robot or Persona knee. All major robotic platforms (VELYS, Mako, ROSA, CORI) deliver excellent outcomes in experienced hands; we standardised on VELYS because it is imageless (no pre-op CT, no extra radiation) and integrates tightly with the globally proven Attune implant. If you have specific clinical reasons to consider a Zimmer implant or wish to compare brands, please book a consultation with Dr. Hardik Shah or Dr. Swagat Shah."},
      {q:"Why doesn't VELYS need a CT scan?", a:"VELYS uses intra-operative anatomy mapping. During surgery, specialised probes register your knee's bone landmarks and ligament tension in real time, and the software builds a personalised surgical plan on the spot. This eliminates pre-op CT cost, scheduling delays, and radiation exposure."},
